From fe43429a8535b6afe4e185699e07db42523eb46f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:07:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Give a STA joining during a group rekey the group keys in
 use

During a group rekey the new GTK, IGTK and BIGTK are not installed until
every STA has completed the Group Key Handshake (SETKEYS), but a STA that
joined in that window got the new keys in EAPOL-Key msg 3/4, the FT
Reassociation Response or the FILS/EPPKE Key Delivery. Group frames, and
with beacon protection every Beacon frame, were protected with keys it
did not have until the AP switched: a STA verifying Beacon frames saw
none valid and disconnected, which is how a STA joining a BSS whose rekey
waited on an unresponsive STA lost its connection seconds later.

Give a joining STA the keys in use (GM) during the rekey, and once it is
in PTKINITDONE start the Group Key Handshake for it, like for the other
STAs, whenever the keys it got are not the current ones. That also covers
a STA whose keys a rekey replaced while it was still joining, which the
rekey skips because it is not yet in PTKINITDONE.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
